Invoking: `write_rule` with `{'rule_name': 'rule_cover_page_numeric_share_spans', 'code': 'def rule_cover_page_numeric_share_spans(doc: dict) -> list[dict]:\n    """Retrieve page 1-2 cover-page body spans tied to common-stock outstanding disclosures, including adjacent numeric-only spans."""\n    try:\n        import re\n        texts = doc.get("texts", []) or []\n        out = []\n        n = len(texts)\n        for i, span in enumerate(texts):\n            if span.get("label") != "text":\n                continue\n            if span.get("page_no") not in (1, 2):\n                continue\n            txt = (span.get("text") or "")\n            path = ((span.get("structure") or {}).get("path_text") or "")\n            hay = f"{path} {txt}".lower()\n            is_numericish = bool(re.fullmatch(r"[\\$\\s,0-9\\.]+", txt.strip())) and any(ch.isdigit() for ch in txt)\n            direct = (\n                "issued and outstanding" in hay\n                or "shares of our common stock" in hay\n                or "shares of common stock" in hay\n                or "common stock outstanding" in hay\n                or "number of shares of common stock outstanding" in hay\n                or "number of shares outstanding" in hay\n            )\n            nearby = False\n            if is_numericish:\n                for j in (i-3, i-2, i-1, i+1, i+2, i+3):\n                    if 0 <= j < n:\n                        s2 = texts[j]\n                        if s2.get("label") != "text":\n                            continue\n                        if s2.get("page_no") != span.get("page_no"):\n                            continue\n                        p2 = ((s2.get("structure") or {}).get("path_text") or "")\n                        t2 = (s2.get("text") or "")\n                        h2 = f"{p2} {t2}".lower()\n                        if (\n                            "common stock outstanding" in h2\n                            or "shares of common stock" in h2\n                            or "shares of our common stock" in h2\n                            or "issued and outstanding" in h2\n                            or "number of shares" in h2\n                        ):\n                            nearby = True\n                            break\n            if direct or nearby:\n                out.append(span)\n        return out\n    except Exception:\n        return []\n'}`
responded: The misses are structural variants of the same cover-page pattern:
- Amazon 2016/2018: label with the phrase is separate from the numeric answer in the next span.
- Nike: answer is a bare number under a cover-page path with “As of ... number of shares ...” in nearby sibling spans.
- Lockheed/Amcor: wording uses “issued and outstanding” / “shares of our common stock”.
I’ll add a targeted broader cover-page rule that captures page 1–2 body text under cover-page/company paths when the text or path mentions issued/outstanding/common stock, plus numeric-only spans in those same cover-page contexts.

